# Nimble Brigand: 1/3; "This creature can't be blocked if you've committed a crime this turn." and "Whenever this creature deals combat
# damage to a player, draw a card." Bot1 casts it on turn 1 with Black Lotus; Bot2 has an Ornithopter. T3: Bot1's Lightning Bolt at itself is
# no crime (nothing of an opponent's is targeted), so the Ornithopter blocks, and combat damage to a creature draws nothing. T5: a Bolt at
# Bot2 is a crime, the block is refused, the Brigand deals 1 to Bot2 and Bot1 draws. T7: the crime of turn 5 is over, so the Ornithopter
# blocks again, and a Bolt at Bot2 after blockers are declared is a crime that does not undo the block (509.1b; ruling 2024-04-12).

